DOCUMENT();
loadMacros(
"PGstandard.pl",
"MathObjects.pl",
"PGML.pl"
);
Context("Numeric");

$fun_2 = Formula("(e^(x))^5");
$fun_1 = Formula("sin((x-8))");

Context("Interval");

$set_ans_4 = Compute("(3, infinity) - ((-infinity, infinity) - {-6, -3, -1, 1, 5, 8}) - ((-infinity, infinity) - {-6, -3, -1, 1, 5, 8})");
$set_ans_5 = Compute("{-6, -3, -1, 1, 5, 8} - ((-infinity, infinity) - {-6, -3, -1, 1, 5, 8}) - ((-infinity, infinity) - (3, infinity))");
$set_ans_6 = Compute("({-6, -3, -1, 1, 5, 8}) U ((3, infinity) U {-6, -3, -1, 1, 5, 8} U ({-6, -3, -1, 1, 5, 8} U (3, infinity)) - ((-infinity, infinity) - ({-6, -3, -1, 1, 5, 8} - ((-infinity, infinity) - (({-6, -3, -1, 1, 5, 8}) U (3, infinity)))))) U {-6, -3, -1, 1, 5, 8}");
$set_ans_1 = Compute("{1, 2, 4, 9} U {1, 2, 4, 9} U ({1, 7} U {1, 7})");
$set_ans_2 = Compute("{1, 7} - ((-infinity, infinity) - {1, 7}) - ((-infinity, infinity) - {1, 2, 4, 9})");
$set_ans_3 = Compute("{1, 2, 4, 9} - ((-infinity, infinity) - {1, 7}) - ((-infinity, infinity) - (({1, 7}) U {1, 2, 4, 9}))");

Context("Vector");

BEGIN_PGML
# Questions:

_For arithmetic problems, if the result is not an integer, then retain *three significant digits*._

What is the value of [`18+9+2-11`]? [_____]{Real(18.)}
---

What is the value of [`5/1+16*17`]? [_____]{Formula('277')}
---

Given the sets:
- [`A = \{1, 2, 4, 9\}`]
- [`B = \{1, 7\}`]

Compute:
- [`A \cup A \cup (B \cup B) = `] [_____]{$set_ans_1}
- [`B \cap B \cap A = `] [_____]{$set_ans_2}
- [`A \cap B \cap ((B) \cup A) = `] [_____]{$set_ans_3}

---

Given the sets:
- [`A = \{-6, -3, -1, 1, 5, 8\}`]
- [`B = \{x | x > 2\}`]

Compute:
- [`B \cap A \cap A = `] [_____]{$set_ans_4}
- [`A \cap A \cap B = `] [_____]{$set_ans_5}
- [`(A) \cup (B \cup A \cup (A \cup B) \cap (A \cap ((A) \cup B))) \cup A = `] [_____]{$set_ans_6}

---

Suppose the vectors:
- [` \vec{u} = \langle -6, -7, -8 \rangle `]
- [` \vec{v} = \langle -5, -4, -6 \rangle `]

Compute:
- [` \vec{v} \times \vec{u} = `] [_____]{Compute("<-5, -4, -6>") x Compute("<-6, -7, -8>")}
- [` \vec{u} \cdot \vec{v} = `] [_____]{Compute("<-6, -7, -8>") . Compute("<-5, -4, -6>")}
- [` \left\| \vec{u} \right\| = `] [_____]{norm(Compute("<-6, -7, -8>"))}
- [` \vec{v} \cdot \vec{u} = `] [_____]{Compute("<-5, -4, -6>") . Compute("<-6, -7, -8>")}

---

Suppose the vectors:
- [` \vec{u} = \langle 7, -10, -6 \rangle `]
- [` \vec{v} = \langle 5, 2, 4 \rangle `]
- [` \vec{w} = \langle -10, 6, 6 \rangle `]

Compute:
- [` \left\| \vec{u} \right\| = `] [_____]{norm(Compute("<7, -10, -6>"))}
- Enter a vector parallel to [` \vec{u} `]. [_____]{Compute("<7, -10, -6>")->cmp(parallel=>1)}
- Enter a unit vector in the direction of [` \vec{v} `]. [_____]{unit(Compute("<5, 2, 4>"))}
- [` \vec{w} \times \vec{u} = `] [_____]{Compute("<-10, 6, 6>") x Compute("<7, -10, -6>")}
- [` \vec{v} \cdot \vec{w} = `] [_____]{Compute("<5, 2, 4>") . Compute("<-10, 6, 6>")}
- [` \vec{u} \times \vec{v} = `] [_____]{Compute("<7, -10, -6>") x Compute("<5, 2, 4>")}

---

Given this function:

>> [`[$fun_1]`] <<

Compute:
- [`f'(2) =`] [_____]{$fun_1->D()->eval(x=>2)}
- [`f'(9) =`] [_____]{$fun_1->D()->eval(x=>9)}
- [`f''(x) =`] [_____]{$fun_1->D()->D()}
- [`f'(x) =`] [_____]{$fun_1->D()}

---

Given this function:

>> [`[$fun_2]`] <<

Compute:
- [`f''(x) =`] [_____]{$fun_2->D()->D()}
- [`f'(1) =`] [_____]{$fun_2->D()->eval(x=>1)}
- [`f'(7) =`] [_____]{$fun_2->D()->eval(x=>7)}
- [`f'(x) =`] [_____]{$fun_2->D()}

---
END_PGML
ENDDOCUMENT();
